---
title: Quick start
description: From a minimal viewer to a reader with find, highlights and citation cards.
---

<script lang="ts">
	import { Demo, Callout, Steps, Step } from '#lib/index.ts';
</script>

<Steps>
	<Step title="Load and show a document">

`Document.Root` loads the PDF; `Viewer.Root` owns zoom, layout and navigation; `Viewer.Viewport` scrolls; `Viewer.Pages` renders every page with a canvas and a text layer.

```svelte
<script>
	import { Document, Viewer } from 'svelte-pdf-mini';
	import 'svelte-pdf-mini/styles.css';
</script>

<Document.Root src="https://arxiv.org/pdf/1706.03762">
	<Viewer.Root zoomMode="page-width" style="height: 100dvh">
		<Viewer.Viewport style="height: 100%">
			<Viewer.Pages />
		</Viewer.Viewport>
	</Viewer.Root>
</Document.Root>
```

	</Step>
	<Step title="Choose the page layers">

Render pages yourself to pick their layers. Each layer is optional.

```svelte
<Viewer.Pages>
	{#snippet children({ pageNumber })}
		<Viewer.Page {pageNumber}>
			<Viewer.Canvas />
			<Viewer.TextLayer />
			<Viewer.LinkLayer />
			<Viewer.Focus />
		</Viewer.Page>
	{/snippet}
</Viewer.Pages>
```

	</Step>
	<Step title="Add a toolbar">

Controls are parts too, so they read the viewer from context. Bind any state you need.

```svelte
<Viewer.Root bind:page bind:zoom>
	<header>
		<PageNav.Prev /> <PageNav.Input /> <PageNav.Next />
		<Zoom.Out /> <Zoom.Select /> <Zoom.In />
	</header>
	<Viewer.Viewport>…</Viewer.Viewport>
</Viewer.Root>
```

	</Step>
	<Step title="Annotate and read like a researcher">

Wrap the pages with `Find.Root`, `Annotations.Root` and `Paper.Root`, add their layers to each page and their floating parts anywhere inside.

```svelte
<Find.Root>
	<Annotations.Root bind:annotations>
		<Paper.Root>
			<Viewer.Viewport>
				<Viewer.Pages>
					{#snippet children({ pageNumber })}
						<Viewer.Page {pageNumber}>
							<Viewer.Canvas />
							<Viewer.TextLayer />
							<Find.Layer />
							<Paper.Layer />
							<Annotations.Layer />
						</Viewer.Page>
					{/snippet}
				</Viewer.Pages>
			</Viewer.Viewport>
			<Annotations.SelectionMenu />
			<Annotations.Popover />
			<Paper.CitationCard />
		</Paper.Root>
	</Annotations.Root>
</Find.Root>
```

	</Step>
</Steps>

The full reader below combines everything on this site — open the source tabs to see how.

<Demo example="reader" height={640} />

<Callout type="tip">
	Every root exposes its state class: <code>bind:viewer</code>, <code>bind:store</code>, <code>bind:paper</code>, <code>bind:find</code>. Use them for commands like <code>viewer.focus(&#123; dest: 'section.3' &#125;)</code> or <code>store.exportPdf()</code>.
</Callout>
